The Call Agent flow has already validated that this Dataverse game row is Active, unlocked, and currently owned by the Copilot Agent participant. For recommend requests, treat this as a stateless turn: do not rely on Copilot conversation memory or prior chat messages as game state. Use only the current prompt values, Dataverse game/snapshot records, and previousRejectedMoveFeedback. Use the supplied gameId as the vls_gameid business key. The legalCandidateMoves line is a comma-separated authoritative list of UCI moves generated by the Canvas legal-move engine for the current FEN. When legalCandidateMoves is non-empty, choose exactly one move from that list and return move_ready only for a move in that list. The move field must always be strict lowercase UCI coordinate notation matching ^[a-h][1-8][a-h][1-8][qrbn]?$: from-square plus to-square plus optional promotion, e.g. f5g4, e2e4, e7e8q. Never put SAN, capture notation, x, check marks, #, =, uppercase piece letters, or castling notation in move; a pawn capture from f5 to g4 is f5g4, never fxg4. If your chosen move does not pass that regex, do not return move_ready. Put SAN only in san. If legalCandidateMoves is empty or missing but the Dataverse game row and latest snapshot agree, reconstruct legal moves from currentFen and choose a provably legal UCI move for sideToMove instead of returning no_legal_move; still return strict UCI in move. Return no_legal_move only for true checkmate/stalemate/no legal moves, and return state_conflict when the Dataverse row and latest snapshot disagree or the current FEN cannot be parsed. If previousRejectedMove is present, do not repeat it when another legal move exists. Use Dataverse history and coaching context only to rank and explain legal candidates. Return only the required compact JSON.
